window.BIOS = {
"Abeer Adel": "An Egyptian Visual Artist, graduate of Fine Arts, Helwan University. The women always endures the weight of the responsibilities expected of her. With a family, she is destracted. by multiple topics going through her head, while multitasking, can make her forgetful of the most basic of things. Just like a fish, long term memory starts to seem like an unrealistic fantasy. That’s how life is!",
"Afraa Ahmed": "(b.1992, Aden, Yemen), currently based in Cairo, is a multi-disciplinary artist whose work includes installation, sculpture، photography and video.",
"Agnes Michalczyk": "A visual artist and educator living and working in Cairo. Graduated from Academy of Visual Arts in Leipzig she taught 2012-2019 at the Faculty of Applied Sciences and Arts at the German University in Cairo. Her work is exploring the urban space of Cairo through a female perspective.",
"Aya Gamil": "Holds aBachelor Degree In Fine arts from Helwan University In Cairo; graduated excellent with honors, ranked 2nd . Her masters degree is in progress and she’s currently a freelance painter.",
"Dalia Negm": "Dalia Negm is a teacher assistant at the Faculty of Fine Arts, Mansoura University, Graphic Department - She holds a Master’s degree in Fine Arts- Graphic department from Helwan University in 2020.",
"Doaa ElDemerdash": "Egyptian Artist born in Kuwait Graduated from Graphic Department ,Faculty of Fine Arts-Helwan University in 2011. Fish is well known for its short memory, and as I became a mother with so many responsibilities and sleep deprivation, it became harder for me to remember or recall even the smallest and easiest things, so I have that feeling of having a fish inside my head that comes and goes and replaced my memory with its short term memory.",
"Eman Hussin": "Born in 1989. Eman Hussin is a visual artist whose works of art harkens back to ancient traditions of a bygone era. Using traditional and experimental printmaking techniques, Her inspiration from the past and its importance in our advancement towards the future.",
"Ghada Waleed": "My art name is ghada zart. I’ve loved drawing since my childhood and it’s been the only way I’ve been able to get rid of reality, simple commitments, and anger.",
"Haidy Mohamed": "Born in Cairo in 1996, holds a BA from the Faculty of Fine Arts, Graphic Department, Printed Design Division, 2019.",
"Hoda Hisham": "Visual artist and freelance photographer. Graduated from Faculty of Fine Arts, Mural painting department, senior 2020.",
"Hossam AbulEla": "Born in Cairo in 1962, holds a Bachelor’s degree in Dramatic Arts - Academy of Arts, Postgraduate Diploma - Academy of Arts, MA in Drama and Criticism and PhD in Arts from the Academy of Arts with first class honor. Fangs Bronze and granite",
"Kenzy Turky": "Born and raised in Egypt, Kenzy started her art journey since school, as her mother was a fine arts graduate; which fueled her artistic sense and passion from a young age. At the first glance, you may feel like this piece is representing a fictional subject. When in reality, it’s a very close, very real state that we as humans go through on regular basis. I see emotions, I see how deep it affects us, how easily it brings us up and in a second go down. We’re not in control of when we implode, how or why. “Imploded” is a state you might have been through; you’re not on your own. With surrealism having powerful psychoanalytic theories for the unconscious, it was the perfect choice to deliver the message accompanied by an abstract background style. The use of abstract in the background is to highlight zoning out from reality with its scattered pressures and challenges. To the “imploded” reality is nothing but a hazy screen.",
"Lana Gul": "Syrian visual artist createing surreal, tonal artworks reflecting her experiences with displacement. She explore themes of identity and longing, offering a poignant commentary on.",
"Mahi Tarek": "An Egyptian visual artist, Graduated from the faculty of fine Arts, Interior design department (2006). She participated in many exhibitions in Egypt, and in the USA.",
"Manar Magdy": "Egyptian illustrator and visual artist, graduated from faculty of applied arts decoration department 2017. A carpet designer at oriental weavers and children book illustrator for 5 years.",
"Mayar Attia": "A Berlin-based Egyptian photographer and filmmaker that graduated from MET Film School Berlin in 2020. History is all around us. However, we choose what gets to be preserved and what doesn›t. Throughout these photographs, you may think it›s just an abandoned building in the forest, but you’re exploring what was formerly known as, “Heilstätte Grabowsee”; the world’s first Tuberculosis-Sanatorium clinic that has survived both the first and second world wars, as well as the Soviet Occupation. 124 years later; the paint on the walls is chipping away, the air is filled with dust, the curtains are merely holding on by a thread... every room you walk into is a reminder of",
"Mostafa Hedayat": "Mostafa Hedayat is a A Visual Artist (B.1978 Cairo, Egypt), Holds BFA & MFA Degrees In Fine Arts (specialization in painting). Currently he is studying PhD at the Faculty of Fine Arts (Department of Painting).",
"Nashwa Ata": "Nashwa Ata: Born in Cairo 1989. Master of Fine Arts 2018, and a PHD candidate. A faculty member at many Arts and Design faculties. Participated in many.",
"Omar Hegazy": "A multidisciplinary visual artist born in 2003, lives in Cairo and studies oil painting at the Faculty of Fine Arts in Zamalek. Hegazy is deeply involved in the contemporary and conceptual art movements. He explores various media and focuses on self-expression, documentation, and popular culture’s impact on individuals.",
"Rana Samir": "Born 1995, and class of 2018 Fine Arts graduate. Rana depends on illustration and explores a variety of mediums, using ready-mades, crafts, and video. She finds a great deal of inspiration in her personal life experiences, past and present, surroundings and people.",
"Safinaz Farouk": "Born in Cairo 1972 Safinaz aka “Safi” started out her career endeavor with 15+ years where she roamed the globe and lived in Dubai, Lebanon and Switzerland. In 2019, she embarked on a journey of self exploration and decided to pursue her natural talent and true passion: Art.",
"Sara Hegazy": "The nickname is Sarah Hegazy, visual artist, born in Cairo 1995 , graduated from the Notre Dame des apotres Ahmed Said, Cairo 2013, I graduated from the Faculty of Fine Arts, Helwan University, mural painting department",
"Soha El Mosly": "Born on 1989, Soha is a Egyptian Cairo based visual artist who received BA from the Fine Arts Faculty of Helwan University in 2011 and MFA in 2018.",
"Tamer Sayed": "Tamer Sayed, born in Cairo in 1982, holds a BA in Art Education, Faculty of Specific Education, Ain Shams University, 2005.",
"Alaa Aboelhamd": "Alaa Abu el-Hamd was born in Qena in 1979. He is an assistant professor in the Department of Painting at the Faculty of Fine Arts in Luxor and has participated in numerous exhibitions in Cairo, Port Said, Alexandria and Luxor since 2000.",
"Heba Tarek": "Heba Tarek was born in 1999 in Cairo and is currently studying Advertising in Helwan University. Heba is a vibrant artist that experiments with collage art, she is going through or a cultural topic that she wants to discuss. Her form of art allows her to get her point across by creating art where her feelings are embodied and then others can see life through her eyes.",
"Omar Senada": "An independent visual artist , curator and cultural program coordinator at the Museum of Fine Arts of Alexandria, Egypt. studied painting at the Faculty of Fine Arts in Alexandria and trained as a teaching assistant at the same university. He made Independent study Mass Alexandria for contemporary art, Alexandria, Egypt 2016, He had a Training at MADRASSA, collaborated with L’Atelier de l’Observatoire Casablanca, Morocco 2017, He holds master degree in fine arts 2020.",
"Rana Hemdan": "A 26 years old Egyptian architect, self-taught contemporary artist, graphic designer, illustrator, book and album covers designer, sculptor and a TEDx speaker 4 times. Graduated from the Faculty of Engineering Alexandria University in 2021, majoring in architecture and construction.",
"Rana Khalil": "A published, award-winning gallery founder, creative director and visual artist, who is experienced in the various fields of graphic, architecture, and interior design. From attention to detail, made to measure proposals, to a fine tuned final product. Started her art career from a young age, Rana was a part of multiple global contemporary art and photography exhibitions, managing luxury hospitality brands, and leading the interior design team in residential, admin, and commercial projects around the MENA region.",
"Taher Abdelazeem": "A n Egyptian artist interested in the Egyptian environment and its aesthetics (human and place) seeks to bring the distance between the formative art and the recipient from different segments of the audience. He’s holding a Ph.D. in Fine Arts, Decorations Department, 2001. And has been working as a Professor since 2013 at Faculty of Fine Arts, Helwan University. He held a lot of Art Exhibitions locally and abroad.",
"Abanoub Adel": "Abanoub Adel is a visual artist born in 1995, Alexandria, Egypt. His main discipline is painting. Abanoub graduated from faculty of fine arts, Painting department, Alexandria University in 2018. “A diptych of two portraits”",
"Abdoul": "Talented visual artist that explores the intersection of art and technology, shedding light on the impact of information overload and the rise of social media an invitation to contemplate.",
"Ahmed Nagy": "(B. 1980) is an artist, founder and cultural producer, who lives and works in Cairo. He has a BFA form Helwan University (2002) and painting and criticism diploma from the same university (2004). He is cofounder of “Cairo Documenta” and founder and director of “Space for Contemporary Art and Cultural Development”. Nagy has taken part in numerous local and international events since 2000 till now.",
"Aisha Nour": "Graduated faculty of fine arts, painting department, Alexandria university, in July 2022. Participated in many group exhibitions in cultural institutions and art galleries since 2019, such as Pop up exhibition at Shelter art space 2023, Luxor international painting symposium 2022, Youth salon 30 edition at Cairo opera house 2020 and many other exhibitions.",
"Amany Isaac": "Amany Isaac started out as an illustrator for books and other published material, then she branched out to being a story board artist in Tarek Nour Agency, and she has participated in multiple group exhibitions.",
"Amina Ashour": "As an emerging digital artist and practicing architect, I find inspiration in the ordinary elements of our daily lives. Through my art, I aim to illuminate the beauty and stories hidden within people, places, and objects that are often unnoticed in the rush of our everyday lives. Using digital tools, I transform these mundane subjects into captivating visual journeys, inviting viewers to pause, reflect, appreciate and find beauty in the familiar. My work celebrates the extraordinary within the ordinary, offering a fresh perspective on the world around us.",
"Amira Khalil": "Amira Khalil is a Cairo based Egyptian artist born in 2001. She studies oil painting at the faculty of fine arts. She uses both traditional and digital painting to express her feelings and talk about what she meets in her daily life from struggles to dreams. For her painting is a way of self-expression and a way to discover herself more through artworks that speak her mind and vision.",
"Asmaa Habib": "Her work explores the organic harmony of nature through abstraction. Inspired by the fluidity of plants, greenery, and natural landscapes, her paintings capture the essence of growth, movement, and life.Through her work, Asmaa invites viewers to reconnect with natures rhythms in a deeply personal and emotional way",
"Aya Elhussieny": "A Visual Artist and Director based in Cairo, she enjoys working on her own personal projects and exhibiting her video and photography work at local and international exhibitions.",
"Basmalah Walie": "Graduated with a BFA, painting department at Helwan University of Fine Arts in 2023. She was interested in arts since a young age and she has participated in many exhibitions since 2016.",
"Dina El Karimy": "El Karimy paints to externalize her internal conflicts, insecurities and emotions in an attempt to develop an emotive language that is able to",
"Ehab Farrag": "Visual artist from Alexandria who participated in many exhibitions.",
"Eslam Saif El-Nasr": "Egyptian visual artist, who holds a Ph.D. in painting from the faculty of fine arts at Helwan University, Artist with various participations in the art scene since 2019. specialized in teaching contemporary art, Since 2019 Eslam has been a member of the board of directors for “the Egyptian Association of Youth Artists” EAOYA. Eslam has his works in private and public collections all over the globe",
"Esraa Hosny": "Esraa Hosny is an Egyptian Turkish artist specializing in abstract paintings. She holds a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in interior design from Helwan University (2014). She received her Master’s degree from Kocaeli University (2020).",
"Fady George Awad": "Fady George is a visual artist, painter, and illustrator currently studying at the Faculty of Fine Arts, specializing in the Painting Department. With a passion for both oil painting and digital art, Fady’s work showcases a unique blend of traditional and contemporary techniques. Who explores the realms of oil painting and digital artistry. Through his work, he seeks to evoke emotions and create visual narratives that bridge the gap between traditional and modern mediums.",
"Farida Mahdy": "23 years old from Cairo, Egypt. Graduated from Photography and Cinema at faculty of Applied Arts, Helwan University. Featured on Vogue Italia 2 times.",
"Ganna Talaat": "A 24-year-old self-taught visual artist and fine arts graduate, she finds inspiration in everyday life. From the ethereal grace of a floating bag to the patterns of sunlight filtering through trees, or the beauty of dust dancing in sunbeams. The world is a canvas full of creative possibilities.",
"Hazem Elshenawy": "ElShenawy captures emotions and states of being through his sculptures, which uniquely blend fluidity and rigidity. His work explores the dynamic tension between movement and stillness.",
"Injy Usama Kamal": "Figurative artist born in Cairo in 1997 and graduated from the faculty of engineering at Ain Shams University in 2021. She was mentored by Stephen Bauman a previous art instructor at Florence Academy of Fine Arts in Italy and took many local and international fine arts workshops. Now working as a freelance figurative artist and art instructor.",
"Mai Manieh": "Egyptian Visual Artist Based in Cairo. Received her BA from the Faculty of Fine Arts at Helwan University in 2011, and her MFA in 2018, currently works as an Assistant lecturer in the Graphic department of the same faculty. Participated in several group exhibitions.",
"Mariam Essam": "Her work transcends traditional sculpture, exploring the interplay of shadows and light thoughtfully integrating the surrounding environment to evoke a deeper sensory and emotional experience.",
"Mariam Abdelhay": "Her work is characterized by the use of unconventional materials, experimental techniques, and alternative perspectives, inviting viewers to engage with familiar themes in unexpected ways. Through her evolving visual language, Abdelhay seeks to create immersive, thought provoking experiences rooted in both cultural heritage and contemporary sensibilities Mohamed Elmowafy .He creates works that explore the unity of all things Delving into the philosophical connections between sciences, cosmic events, psychology, and emotions, Mowafy transforms ordinary moments into extraordinary experiences, revealing",
"Mohanad Youssef": "Mohanad has a wealth of experience as a visual artist, serving as a teaching assistant at the faculty of fine arts, Assiut University, from October 2019 to July 2022. Currently, he continues his academic journey as a teaching assistant at the faculty of fine arts, Nahda University, Beni Suef, starting from October 2022.",
"Moheeb": "A self taught illustrator, print maker and tattoo artist, known as tezerd based in Cairo. His inspiration always comes from living creatures and their behavior.",
"Nayera Ahmed Fathy": "Egyptian visual artist, born in 1990. She studied painting at the Faculty of Fine Arts, Alexandria University. She currently works as a lecturer at the same university. She obtained her master’s degree in Fine Arts in May 2018 and completed her Ph.D. in May 2023",
"Omnia Mohamed": "Born in Giza in 1992, Egyptian Visual Artist. Received her master’s degree in Painting in February 2023, and she holds a BA from the Faculty of Fine Arts college, Helwan University in 2014. Currently, she is a teaching assistant painting department at the same college.",
"Randa Magdi": "Randa participated in the international AGENDA exhibition at the Bibliotheca Alexandrina for three consecutive years, in 2021, 2022, and 2023. She also took part in a group exhibition at Designopia Zone in Abbasia, titled ‘Visual Arts.’ Her works can be categorized as a documentation of the events, experiences, and people she encounters or weaves through her imagination.",
"Razaz Elsadig": "Razaz is a visual artist and pottery maker. For her art is self-discovery and the creative process is a search for myself in the world around me.",
"Reem Elhefnawy": "Her work explores themes of identity of a peace seeking self, through the simple 2D Universe of comic books. Within the 3D sense of sculpture, she tries to drag the 2D simplicity into our reality, giving us a mashup of a new universe, The Comicverse Yahya KhalilHe creates evocative works that delve into the intricacies of human emotion and introspection. His practice is rooted in a deep sensitivity to the psychological and emotional layers of the human experience, which he translates into compelling visual narratives",
"Suzan Elwakil": "A fine artist from Alexandria, she discovered her passion for drawing and fine art in childhood but began serious artistic practice upon joining the Faculty of Fine Arts. Art serves as a means to channel her energy and capture emotions on a tangible canvas, providing a space for creative freedom. Starting with academic studies, her interest in portraiture, particularly self-portraits and selfies, grew steadily. This smooth and expressive form became a way for her to convey emotions.",
"Adam Shafik": "Adam Shafik is a rising multidisciplinary artist currently studying creative media production. Through visual storytelling and multimedia expressions, he captures the nuanced relationships between individuals and their environments, and prompts reflection on the significance attached to material possessions as vessels of memory and identity.",
"Mahmoud El Masry": "Born in 1998 , graduated from The faculty of art education-Helwan university in 2022. Member of The syndicate of fine artists. Participated in numerous exhibitions and events including:”Egypt International Art Carnival” in Hurghada, 2022 “Rose and Vanilla” Exhibition at Arcan Plaza, 2022 “Youth World Arts” Exhibition in Hurghada, 2022 “Agenda” Exhibition 14th and 15th session at Alexandria Library",
"Mahmoud Sami": "Mahmoud Sami, born in 1997, is an Egyptian visual artist with a Bachelor’s degree in Art Education from Helwan University. His artistic journey has been marked by participation in various exhibitions, showcasing his talent and commitment to the craft. Notable events include the Farouk Hosny Foundation for Culture and Arts competition in 2022, Salon Al Shabab 29 and 31.",
"Rania Abu Elazm": "Egyptian visual artist -Lecturer in faculty of fine arts",
"Yasmine Mazen": "Born in 1999, Yasmine holds a Bachelor’s degree in Art Education, graduating in 2023. Currently pursuing a Master’s degree in the Faculty of Art Education, she passionately explores the intersections of education and art. A dedicated researcher, Yasmine is committed to advancing the field of art education.",
"Nagat Farouk": "Graduated with a bachelor in art education from Helwan University in 1987, and I obtained Master’s and doctorate degrees in art education from Helwan University.",
"MennaAllah Raafat": "MennaAllah Raafat is an independent artist who got diagnosed with leukemia cancer back in 2022. Despite what she was going through, was able to transform her anxiety, fear, and the sorrows of illness into the energy of art. It overflew with melodies and paths of hope, touching roses with their brilliant colors and various textures. In the end, it presented a world of joy and radiance in painting artwork of a world whispering and weeping with optimism that transcends its current reality.",
"Mahmoud Marey": "Mahmoud Marey was born in 1982 and acquired his Bachelor’s degree in Art Education from Al-Azhar University. He is a member of the Syndicate of plastic arts, Cairo Atelier, and El Lakta El Wahda Artists.He participated in 31 Group Exhibitions and held 9 Solo Exhibitions.",
"Mahitab Elshafie": "Teacher at faculty of applied arts helwan university, Master and PHD degree about using the waste materials in art and the eclectic thoughts .",
"OP": "We take immense pleasure in unveiling the arrival of a prominent Italian Egyptian artist to our esteemed community, presenting a novel and distinctive artistic approach. The artist’s creations exemplify a profound complexity and dynamic energy, contributing significantly to the vibrant landscape of contemporary arts. It is with great anticipation and reverence that we introduce, with utmost pride, The Art and its transformative influence on our collective creative journey.",
"Mirna Isac": "born in 1998, graduated from the Faculty of Fine Arts, Alexandria University in 2022, participated in many exhibitions and competitions, and won the artist Hassan Heshmat Award,the Vanguards Competitionthe centenary session of the Association of Fine Arts Lovers 2022, and obtained a certificate of encouragement from the Visual Arts Salon for Youth session The ninth in the Creativity Center in Alexandria2023.",
"Nada Hassanien": "Nada Hassanien, An Egyptian visual artist and graphic designer. I am 26 years.graduated from faculty of commerce English section and Fine arts ( free studies).I participated in the youth Salon in 2022.am passionate about art, collage.Seeking for unleashing the beauty of everything through using art.",
"Gabal": "Born in 1999, Mohamed AboGabal is a self-taught visual artist and photographer, based in Cairo. He previously served as an Artist Assistant in Sawa workshops at Townhouse Gallery (2019). He has a keen interest in experimenting with a range of art mediums , although his primary focus is on pop art and paleontology as a research field.",
"Wessam Wafik": "Wessam Wafik is a multidisciplinary visual artist based in Cairo, Egypt. Graduated from Faculty of Arts & Design. Wessam mostly works and experiments with printmaking, illustration, paper-making & alternative photographic techniques, in addition to the creation and merging of different types of artforms with the goal of developing an authentic mixture of ‘Process and Product’.",
"Samah El Shamy": "Visual artist and journalistic illustrator. Born in Gharbia in 1989, she holds a Bachelor’s degree in Fine Arts in 2011, Helwan University, a member of the Fine Artists Syndicate, a member of the Fine Arts Lovers Association.",
"Kamila Bassioni": "Kamila Bassioni is an Egyptian-Irish visual artist and freelance illustrator born in Dublin 1985, She received her B.A. in scenography from the fine arts college in Egypt 2009.",
"Amani Moussa": "An Egyptian artist, born in Cairo in 1991. Holds a Bachelor’s degree in Fine Arts, Graphics Department, Helwan University.",
"Miriam Hanna": "Miriam Saieed Hanna (b. 1999, Cairo, Egypt) is a multidisciplinary artist practicing visual art, concept art, and art direction, alongside her musical talents. Graduating from the Faculty of Fine Arts in 2022, majoring in Scenography and Set Design, she engages in the art scene, showcasing her work in notable exhibitions.",
"Adham Aboudoma": "Growing up in an artistic family shaped his creative perspective, leading to an art practice that merges fine art with the conceptual rigor of design. His work reflects on the tension between personal identity and societal constraints, exploring the subconscious in everyday life through painting, mixed media, and dark humor",
"Aya Salah": "A sculptor and visual artist known for her expressive and surrealist approach. Her work explores symbolic and emotional themes through sculptural forms that reflect the human experience. She views art as a transformative tool, one that transcends materiality to become a space for dialogue, self discovery, and connection",
"Hamas Sabahy": "Her work draws on the social, political, and emotional dynamics of daily life. Using symbolism; animal figures, hybrid forms, and surreal compositions, she expresses inner conflict and silent tension between individuals and surrounding systems. Her art navigates the space between reality and imagination, the personal and collective, the mythical and political"
};
